  "entry": "code/index.html",
  "notes": "Found in a public repository and run by a computer-use agent (batch public-1). Rotate and translate an MRI NIfTI volume by hand in three orthogonal views until it lines up with the anatomical axes. Draw a crop box around the brain. Export the affine matrix, the crop box and the reoriented, cropped NIfTI. The browser tool is the interactive half of the workflow. The downstream half is the companion script reorient.py, which takes the input file, the saved matrix, the saved selection and an output file and repeats the same transform outside the browser. This run did not exercise reorient.py. Data used in the run: example. tree.json is the workflow the agent did and a second agent replayed; run.json says how.",
